WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.077 --> 00:00:18.726
I've heard great inventors dream up ideas in their sleep.

2
00:00:19.846 --> 00:00:22.228
I don't know if I dreamed my idea that night.

3
00:00:25.249 --> 00:00:29.352
But when I woke up early the next morning, I had the answer to Jenny's problem.

4
00:00:30.472 --> 00:00:32.774
And the answer wasn't under my nose.

5
00:00:33.854 --> 00:00:35.976
It was on top of Jenny's nose!

6
00:00:38.197 --> 00:00:40.478
It was Saturday, so we didn't have school.

7
00:00:41.819 --> 00:00:43.600
I jumped out of bed and got dressed.

8
00:00:46.362 --> 00:00:49.604
Then I dashed downstairs, and knocked on Josh and Jenny's door.

9
00:00:52.186 --> 00:00:53.106
No one answered.

10
00:00:54.487 --> 00:00:55.208
I knocked harder.

11
00:00:56.840 --> 00:00:57.720
Finally Mr.

12
00:00:57.800 --> 00:01:01.042
Chen came to the door, wearing his pajamas and bathrobe.

13
00:01:02.682 --> 00:01:04.223
Josh and Jenny stood behind him.

14
00:01:04.243 --> 00:01:06.564
"Jenny!" I cried.

15
00:01:06.584 --> 00:01:09.865
"I figured out why you're having trouble in school!"

16
00:01:09.885 --> 00:01:16.028
"Why?" asked Jenny, yawning and rubbing her eyes.

17
00:01:16.048 --> 00:01:19.089
"Because you can't see!"

18
00:01:19.109 --> 00:01:20.169
I said.

19
00:01:20.189 --> 00:01:23.331
"That's true," said Jenny.

20
00:01:23.351 --> 00:01:26.792
"You woke me up, Iggy!

21
00:01:26.832 --> 00:01:30.854
My eyes are still half-closed."

22
00:01:30.874 --> 00:01:32.234
"No!" I insisted.

23
00:01:32.254 --> 00:01:33.955
"That's not it.

24
00:01:34.395 --> 00:01:36.716
Remember when you tripped over the dog leash?"

25
00:01:38.257 --> 00:01:39.057
Jenny nodded.

26
00:01:39.077 --> 00:01:40.818
"I didn't even see it."

27
00:01:40.838 --> 00:01:45.760
"And you didn't want to call out numbers for the slide," I said.

28
00:01:45.780 --> 00:01:48.121
"Because you couldn't read them."

29
00:01:49.581 --> 00:01:50.522
Jenny blinked at me.

30
00:01:52.402 --> 00:01:54.063
Mr. Chen was squinting too.

31
00:01:54.843 --> 00:01:56.064
He looked confused.

32
00:01:57.176 --> 00:01:58.537
"I don't understand, Iggy.

33
00:01:59.618 --> 00:02:02.000
Jenny just got new glasses a few months ago."

34
00:02:02.020 --> 00:02:05.784
"And they work perfectly," said Jenny.

35
00:02:05.804 --> 00:02:10.268
"Yes, your glasses worked perfectly," I said.

36
00:02:10.288 --> 00:02:13.671
"But you haven't been wearing your glasses."

37
00:02:13.691 --> 00:02:16.593
"What do you mean?"

38
00:02:17.114 --> 00:02:17.874
asked Jenny.

39
00:02:17.894 --> 00:02:22.118
"Remember when you said you and Sara had the same glasses?"

40
00:02:23.199 --> 00:02:23.920
Jenny nodded.

41
00:02:25.168 --> 00:02:26.929
"Our glasses are the same color.

42
00:02:27.429 --> 00:02:28.950
But our eyes are very different.

43
00:02:30.270 --> 00:02:32.151
Sara can't see things close up.

44
00:02:32.531 --> 00:02:34.552
And I can't see things far away."

45
00:02:34.572 --> 00:02:37.194
"Right!" I said.

46
00:02:37.214 --> 00:02:41.576
"And you said Sara is having trouble in school now too."

47
00:02:41.596 --> 00:02:45.557
"Yes," said Jenny.

48
00:02:45.577 --> 00:02:50.800
"So?" "So your glasses probably got switched," I said.

49
00:02:51.864 --> 00:02:55.306
"I think you're wearing Sara's glasses and she's wearing yours!"

50
00:02:58.148 --> 00:03:00.729
By now Jenny's eyes were wide-open.

51
00:03:00.749 --> 00:03:03.211
"I think you're right!"

52
00:03:03.611 --> 00:03:04.211
she said.

53
00:03:04.231 --> 00:03:07.913
"We were both crying when we said good-bye.

54
00:03:08.934 --> 00:03:10.715
So we had to take off our glasses.

55
00:03:12.036 --> 00:03:14.017
They must have gotten switched then."

56
00:03:14.037 --> 00:03:16.758
"Jenny," said Mr.

57
00:03:16.838 --> 00:03:19.580
Chen. "Can you go get your glasses?"

58
00:03:23.148 --> 00:03:24.989
Jenny got her glasses and put them on.

59
00:03:25.869 --> 00:03:26.409
Then Mr.

60
00:03:26.489 --> 00:03:28.149
Chen held up a newspaper.

61
00:03:28.169 --> 00:03:30.470
"Can you read this?"

62
00:03:31.190 --> 00:03:34.071
he asked, stepping back and pointing to a headline.

63
00:03:35.391 --> 00:03:37.052
Jenny peered at the newspaper.

64
00:03:37.072 --> 00:03:39.553
"No," she said.

65
00:03:39.573 --> 00:03:44.094
"The letters look blurry."

66
00:03:44.114 --> 00:03:48.335
"Then Iggy is right!"

67
00:03:48.835 --> 00:03:49.615
said Josh.

68
00:03:50.616 --> 00:03:51.876
Mr. Chen smiled.

69
00:03:52.772 --> 00:03:53.853
He looked relieved.

70
00:03:55.254 --> 00:03:56.556
"Iggy, that was amazing!

71
00:03:56.936 --> 00:03:59.038
You are a true problem-solver."

72
00:03:59.058 --> 00:04:02.181
"Thanks!" I said, grinning.

73
00:04:03.262 --> 00:04:06.004
"Let's have pancakes to celebrate," said Mr.

74
00:04:06.084 --> 00:04:11.629
Chen. "After breakfast I'll call Sara's mom and dad and tell them about what happened."

75
00:04:15.353 --> 00:04:18.696
That afternoon Jenny and Sara met and switched glasses.

76
00:04:20.416 --> 00:04:23.717
After that neither of them had any more problems in school.

77
00:04:25.498 --> 00:04:26.519
On Monday Mr.

78
00:04:26.559 --> 00:04:28.759
Bright, the inventor, came to our school.

79
00:04:30.140 --> 00:04:32.341
He showed us some of his latest inventions.

80
00:04:34.082 --> 00:04:36.983
One of them was a little umbrella for a dog.

81
00:04:38.023 --> 00:04:41.785
You could attach it to a dog's collar so the dog wouldn't get wet.

82
00:04:45.126 --> 00:04:49.288
Mr. Bright brought his dog onstage and showed us how it worked.

83
00:04:53.648 --> 00:04:54.849
All the kids loved it.

84
00:04:54.869 --> 00:05:01.731
"I know many of you are good inventors too," said Mr.

85
00:05:01.771 --> 00:05:05.413
Bright. It seemed like he was looking right at me.

86
00:05:06.413 --> 00:05:09.154
He probably loved my Pick-a-Number invention!

87
00:05:09.174 --> 00:05:13.296
"I have been reading your invention ideas," Mr.

88
00:05:13.336 --> 00:05:14.016
Bright went on.

89
00:05:14.036 --> 00:05:18.318
"And I've chosen one to be included in my new book."

90
00:05:19.459 --> 00:05:22.280
Mr. Bright took a piece of paper from his jacket pocket.

91
00:05:23.336 --> 00:05:26.704
I held my breath, waiting for him to call out my name.
